CBR_COLS = ["CBR-ID", "Rule Statement", "Use Case Relevant"]
W = "Withdrawn — "
CBR = [
["CBR-01","A New customer becomes Active as soon as their first membership package or day pass is paid. Paying for a PT package does not change the member state.","UC-20, UC-22, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-02","An Expired member becomes Active again as soon as a new membership package or day pass is paid. Paying for a PT package does not change the member state.","UC-20, UC-22, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-03","When the membership package reaches its end date, an Active member becomes Expired.","UC-19, UC-41"],
["CBR-04","Nobody may edit an Inactive profile. The Receptionist cannot see it, the Manager sees it read-only, and the Admin traces its history through the audit log.","UC-08, UC-16, UC-17"],
["CBR-05","A New customer may buy a first membership package or day pass, but not a PT package (CBR-59).","UC-20, UC-22"],
["CBR-06","An Expired member may buy a new membership package or day pass to continue; buying a PT package requires a valid membership package first (CBR-59).","UC-20, UC-22"],
["CBR-07","The maximum number of freezes per package is configured by the Manager (P-01, default 1) and copied into the subscription at sale.","UC-09, UC-18"],
["CBR-08","The maximum freeze duration is configured by the Manager (P-02, default 1 month).","UC-09, UC-18"],
["CBR-09","Changing a package price or description in the catalogue never applies retroactively to existing orders.","UC-09, UC-20, UC-21, UC-22"],
["CBR-10","The price of an existing order cannot be edited. A wrong order is cancelled and a new one is created.","UC-20, UC-21"],
["CBR-11","The Receptionist may cancel a Paid counter order only within the shift that created it and before the shift is closed; the money is returned to the customer at the counter.","UC-20, UC-25"],
["CBR-12","Every price belongs to a specific package in the catalogue; there are no free-standing prices.","UC-09, UC-10"],
["CBR-13","Customers younger than P-05 (default 10 years) cannot buy a single PT package.","UC-16, UC-21"],
["CBR-14","Customers younger than P-05 (default 10 years) cannot buy or join a couple PT package.","UC-16, UC-21"],
["CBR-15","Customers younger than P-05 (default 10 years) cannot book a single PT session.","UC-21, UC-37"],
["CBR-16","A member who still has a running package or unused PT sessions goes to Pending deletion and waits for Manager approval.","UC-16, UC-17"],
["CBR-17","A customer profile and a login account are separate records. Every Self profile created at the counter gets its account at the same time (CBR-24, CBR-31); a profile without an account is either a Dependent profile or an older Self profile that never received an account, which the customer can claim online (UC-Claim).","UC-04, UC-05, UC-16, UC-20"],
["CBR-18","Only Dependent profiles have no login account. A Self profile always has an email and an account, whatever package it buys (including day passes).","UC-05, UC-16, UC-20, UC-Claim"],
["CBR-19","If the Receptionist enters, in the customer profile form, a phone number that matches an active Person, the system opens that Person's customer profile. If the Person has no customer profile that is not Inactive (for example an employee), the Receptionist checks an identity document and creates the customer profile on the same Person instead of a new Person (CBR-114). On the quick-create form of the sales screen a matching phone number is refused instead (CBR-118).","UC-16, UC-20, UC-IDENT"],
["CBR-20","If a guest signs up with the phone number of an active self-owned profile that has no account and enters the same email as the profile, the system sends a verification code to that email instead of creating a new profile; after the correct code and a password, the account is attached to the existing profile.","UC-05, UC-Claim"],
["CBR-21","A Dependent profile has no login account.","UC-04, UC-05, UC-20"],
["CBR-22","The guardian only needs to be present at registration, not at every session.","UC-16, UC-19"],
["CBR-23","If a phone number matches no active Person (only Inactive ones), a new Person and profile are created normally.","UC-16, UC-IDENT"],
["CBR-24","When the Receptionist creates a Self profile — on the quick-create form of the sales screen or in the customer profile form — the login account is created in the same transaction with the Person's email and a temporary password (CBR-31), whatever package is bought. If the Person already has an account (for example an employee, CBR-19), no second account is created: the existing account now also serves the Customer role (DBR-65).","UC-16, UC-20"],
["CBR-25","A guest signing up with the phone number of a self-owned profile that has no account, but with a different email from the one on the profile, cannot activate it. The system says the phone number is registered with another email (masked); the guest uses that email or asks the Receptionist to verify and update it.","UC-05, UC-Claim"],
["CBR-26","If a guest signs up with the phone number of an active Person that already has a login account, no account or profile is created; the system says the number already has an account and points to Sign In / Forgot Password, without saying whose number it is. An employee who also wants to train as a customer gets the customer profile at the counter (CBR-19), never through online sign-up.","UC-03, UC-05"],
["CBR-27","A self-owned profile without an email cannot be activated online; the customer goes to the counter so the Receptionist can add the email, which creates the account (CBR-24).","UC-05, UC-16, UC-Claim"],
["CBR-28","Duplicate checks during self sign-up only compare against the phone number on Person; guardian numbers recorded on Dependent profiles neither block nor activate anything — the guardian registers as a new customer.","UC-05, UC-IDENT"],
["CBR-29","When the email of an account changes, by the account holder (UC-04) or by the Receptionist (UC-16), the system sends a warning to the old email and signs out every session of that account except the one that made the change. The email is stored on Person, so the change applies to every role of that Person.","UC-04, UC-16"],
["CBR-30","In their own account a customer can change only the avatar (upload or remove), email, phone number and password. Full name, date of birth, check-in photo and guardian details are changed by the Receptionist (UC-16), because they are used for check-in verification and the PT age rule. Email and phone number changes follow CBR-110.","UC-04, UC-16"],
["CBR-31","An account created by the Receptionist (CBR-24) is Active immediately and gets a random temporary password of 10 characters containing at least one letter and one digit, without look-alike characters (0, O, o, 1, l, I); only its BCrypt hash is stored. The system emails the temporary password together with the customer code before the transaction commits; if the email cannot be sent (or takes longer than 10 seconds) nothing is saved — neither the profile nor the account — and MSG04 is shown. The Receptionist sees the masked email in the success toast (MSG122). The customer signs in with email or phone number and the temporary password and may change it later in Account Settings; a change is not forced. The Sign In screen explains this in a hint box. A Dependent profile gets no account and no email (CBR-21).","UC-01, UC-03, UC-04, UC-16, UC-20"],
["CBR-32", "A Dependent profile has no self-service channel: it cannot view schedules, book single sessions, reschedule or cancel PT sessions itself. Packages and single sessions are bought at the counter (UC-20, UC-21, CBR-54); PT sessions are rescheduled by the PT at the guardian's request through session handling (BR-64); schedules are checked with the Receptionist or the PT. Cancellation is not supported — an absent customer's session becomes Missed (CBR-42).", "UC-16, UC-21, UC-35"],
["CBR-33","Before acting at the counter on behalf of a Dependent profile, the Receptionist verifies the requester with one of the guardian phone numbers recorded on the profile (DBR-25) or the customer code. The PT agrees changes with the customer or guardian outside the system before handling a session (BR-63); the system does not ask the PT to verify a phone number.","UC-16, UC-21, UC-35"],
["CBR-34","A paid day pass is valid immediately.","UC-20, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-35","A check-in photo is mandatory for every package except the day pass; the Receptionist takes it at the counter when the customer first buys a package, or at the first check-in (BR-33).","UC-16, UC-19, UC-20"],
["CBR-36","A day pass gives exactly one entry to the gym.","UC-19, UC-20"],
["CBR-37","The avatar uploaded by the customer is for display only and is never used for check-in verification.","UC-04, UC-16, UC-19"],
["CBR-38","The check-in photo belongs to the customer profile, not to the account. Only the Receptionist can take or retake it; the customer cannot change or delete it, even with an account.","UC-04, UC-16, UC-19"],
["CBR-39","When booking a single session online, customers can only choose slots in the current week (today to Sunday); from Saturday, slots of the following week also become available. The Receptionist scheduling a PT package and a PT rescheduling or transferring a session are not bound by this limit.","UC-21, UC-35, UC-37"],
["CBR-40","The hold of an online single-session slot lasts exactly as long as the order's payment deadline (P-09, copied into the order at creation — GBR-04); there is no separate slot timer. A Failed or Expired transaction does not release the slot: the order is still Pending, so the slot stays Held and the customer can pay again within the deadline (CBR-69).","UC-37, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-41","A customer can hold slots for only one Pending single-session order at a time. Creating a new single-session order while an older one is Pending cancels the older order (type: replaced by a new order — CBR-71) and returns its slot to Free.","UC-37, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-42","The PT does not mark attendance. After the session day has ended, JOB-04 (daily 00:05) closes every session still Scheduled: a session on a date declared closed all day → Cancelled / GymClosed (CBR-56); otherwise, if nobody in the session can use the gym that day (CBR-117) and someone is frozen → Missed / MembershipFrozen; if nobody can use the gym and nobody is frozen → Missed / NoMembership; otherwise, if the customer (couple: either member) checked in that day → CheckedIn; otherwise → Missed / NoCheckIn. Each session is closed in its own transaction with an audit line; the slot and commission are not changed. CheckedIn only means the customer entered the gym that day, not that the PT session was confirmed.","UC-31, UC-32, UC-36"],
["CBR-43","A PT package schedule is built from a weekly template: for each weekday Monday–Friday the Receptionist chooses either no session or one start time (1–5 sessions per week), on the chosen PT's slots. Individual dates can be overridden with another time or no session (BR-41). The most frequent start time is stored as the package's fixed start time. Sessions moved later by the PT keep their own time (BR-64, BR-65).","UC-21, UC-35"],
["CBR-44",W+"customers do not swap sessions. The PT moves sessions only to slots they have published (BR-64).","UC-30, UC-38"],
["CBR-45",W+"customers do not swap sessions. A PT rescheduling or transferring a session (BR-64, BR-65) is not restricted to weekdays.","UC-21, UC-38"],
["CBR-46","After a reschedule, transfer or cancellation by the PT, the system immediately sends a bell notification to the customer (couple: both members) whose account is Active, and on a transfer also to the receiving PT. Dependent profiles are informed outside the system.","UC-35, UC-36"],
["CBR-47","The system does not handle the case where one member of a couple package drops out.","UC-21, UC-31"],
["CBR-48","PT packages (single and couple) are not sold online; they are sold at the counter only. Screens that suggest renewing a PT package point the customer to the counter (hotline and opening hours).","UC-21, UC-22, UC-36"],
["CBR-49","Single and couple PT packages are paid at the counter in cash or by bank transfer only. A single session booked online is paid through the online gateway (CBR-53); a single session bought at the counter is paid in cash or by transfer (CBR-54).","UC-21, UC-37, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-50","When a PT package order is Paid, the system creates one Scheduled session for each held date in the same transaction: the held slots become Booked and each session stores its session value and commission (DBR-58, DBR-59).","UC-21, UC-32"],
["CBR-51","The customer cannot change PT midway when the PT is not at fault.","UC-21, UC-35"],
["CBR-52","PT package times are chosen from the PT's published slots. If a chosen time is a slot the PT has not opened on that date, the Receptionist must tick \"Confirmed with PT\" before holding; the system then creates that slot as part of the hold (BR-96).","UC-21, UC-30"],
["CBR-53","Booking a single session: choose a PT → choose a time from the PT's published schedule → the system creates a Pending order and holds the slot immediately (Held — DBR-36) → the customer pays within the order deadline → when the order is Paid the slot becomes Booked and the session is created. If the deadline passes unpaid, the slot returns to Free.","UC-37, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-54", "Selling a single session at the counter: when the customer confirms, the system creates a Pending order and the slot becomes Held immediately for the order's payment deadline (P-09, default 20 minutes, shown as an mm:ss countdown — GBR-27). When the order is Paid the slot becomes Booked and the session is created; if the deadline passes unpaid, the order is Cancelled and the slot returns to Free. A Failed or Expired transaction keeps the slot Held while the order is still within its deadline (CBR-40, CBR-69).", "UC-20, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-55","When a PT package passes its end date, the subscription becomes Expired automatically. Any Scheduled session left in the package (after reschedules or transfers) becomes Cancelled at the same time (PackageExpired), with no refund and no term extension.","UC-21, UC-32, UC-36"],
["CBR-56","Sessions are still generated on a date declared closed (the PT sale screen marks them). Before that date the PT must reschedule them (BR-64, no swap quota used); the PT dashboard lists them and JOB-08 does not remind customers for that day. A session still Scheduled after the closed day is cancelled by JOB-04 as GymClosed: no commission, no make-up, no term extension.","UC-11, UC-21, UC-32, UC-35"],
["CBR-57",W+"merged into CBR-56: a closed day declared after the order is Paid is handled exactly like any other closed day (sessions stay Scheduled for the PT to reschedule).","UC-11, UC-21, UC-32, UC-36"],
["CBR-58","A PT package or a single session only pays for the trainer; it does not include gym access. Gym access comes only from a membership package or a day pass.","UC-19, UC-21, UC-37, UC-41"],
["CBR-59", "A PT package order (single or couple) can be created only for a customer who holds a membership package valid today and is not frozen — a day pass does not count. Otherwise the Receptionist sells a membership package first (UC-20); only after it is Paid is the PT package order created. A Receptionist cannot sell to their own customer profile, and an employee who also trains as a customer must choose a different PT (CBR-115).", "UC-20, UC-21"],
["CBR-60", "A single session can be booked only on a date covered by a valid membership package, or for today if the customer holds a valid day pass (CBR-34, BR-32). A walk-in who wants a single PT session buys today's day pass, then the Receptionist sells today's session at the counter (CBR-54).", "UC-21, UC-37"],
["CBR-61","When the PT reschedules a session (UC-35), a target date on which the customer cannot use the gym (CBR-117) is allowed but highlighted in amber; the session then shows \"needs attention\" and JOB-08 reminds the customer the day before.","UC-35, UC-36"],
["CBR-62","A freeze is never blocked by PT sessions and does not change them when it is saved: future sessions inside the freeze period stay Scheduled and are shown with the warning \"inside the freeze period\" on the customer's and PT's screens. After each session day JOB-04 closes such a session as Missed / MembershipFrozen when nobody in the session could use the gym (CBR-42). The freeze applies only to the membership (BR-21), so the PT package term does not move. Before saving, the system lists the sessions that fall inside the freeze period so the Receptionist can inform the customer.","UC-18, UC-36"],
["CBR-63","A valid day pass counts as gym access for that day, also for PT package sessions (CBR-117). A customer with remaining PT sessions but no valid membership must buy a membership package or a day pass for each session day; otherwise JOB-04 closes the session as Missed / NoMembership.","UC-19, UC-20, UC-36"],
["CBR-64","A PT package session on a day when nobody in it can use the gym (CBR-117) is closed by JOB-04 as Missed / NoMembership (or MembershipFrozen). It is deducted like a no-show (BR-52) and still earns commission (CBR-80). The system neither reschedules the session nor extends the PT package; the customer is reminded the day before (JOB-08).","UC-32, UC-36"],
["CBR-65","The membership does not have to cover the whole PT term: a PT package can be sold as soon as the customer (couple: each member) holds a membership valid today (CBR-59). The customer search on the PT sale screen shows each customer's membership end date (\"gym package until dd/mm\") so the Receptionist can suggest a renewal; sessions that later fall on days without gym access are labelled (CBR-66) and reminded by JOB-08. A PT package still never grants gym access (CBR-58).","UC-19, UC-21"],
["CBR-66","A Scheduled session on a day the customer cannot use the gym (CBR-117) is labelled on the customer's schedule (\"no gym package\" / \"inside freeze period\" / \"gym closed\") and in the PT dashboard \"Needs attention\" block. The label disappears when a membership or day pass covering that day is bought.","UC-19, UC-32, UC-36, UC-41"],
["CBR-67","A couple-package session is closed as Missed for lack of gym access only when both members cannot use the gym that day; if one member is frozen and the other can use the gym, the session follows the normal check-in rule (CBR-42).","UC-18, UC-36"],
["CBR-68","Sessions closed as Missed / MembershipFrozen earn commission like any Missed session (CBR-80); their past slots are not released. Missed is final (DBR-38). If the freeze is cancelled early, sessions after the actual end date simply stay Scheduled.","UC-18, UC-46"],
["CBR-69","When a transaction becomes Failed or Expired the order stays Pending; the customer can pay again for the same order while it is within its deadline.","UC-22, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-70","An online Pending order with no Success transaction by its payment deadline (P-09, default 20 minutes) becomes Cancelled (type: payment deadline passed), and its Pending transaction becomes Expired. Each VNPay payment link is valid for 5 minutes but never beyond the order deadline. Paying after the deadline is refused (MSG146). To buy again the customer creates a new order; price and voucher are re-evaluated.","UC-09, UC-22"],
["CBR-71","When a customer creates a new online order for the same package while an older online order for it is Pending, the older order becomes Cancelled (type: replaced by a new order).","UC-22, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-72","If the gateway reports success but the order is already Cancelled or the amount does not match exactly, the transaction is still recorded as Success, the order is not Paid (if not yet cancelled it becomes Cancelled, type: invalid payment), no entitlement is created, and the transaction goes to the Manager's refund list (BR-81).","UC-26, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-73","A voucher is valid when all of these hold: it is Active, within its validity period, total uses remain, the customer has not exceeded their allowed uses (CBR-74), the order's package type is within the voucher scope (CBR-76), and the package price before discount reaches the minimum order value.","UC-12, UC-20, UC-23"],
["CBR-74","Each customer may use a voucher at most the number of times configured on it (default 1; empty = unlimited). Uses are counted on orders held by the customer that are not Cancelled, including Pending ones; for a couple package only the holder is counted.","UC-12, UC-23"],
["CBR-75","A voucher cannot be added, removed or changed while the order has a Pending transaction.","UC-23, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-76","Each voucher has a scope chosen by the Manager: membership packages & day passes (default) or membership packages only. PT packages and single sessions never accept a voucher; the PT sale screen has no voucher field.","UC-12, UC-21, UC-23"],
["CBR-77","The Receptionist confirms a bank transfer at the counter only after checking that the money has arrived in the gym's account (tick \"received in full\"; optional transfer reference up to 50 characters).","UC-20, UC-21, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-78","The Receptionist can close a shift only when no counter order created in that shift is still Pending: each must be paid or cancelled (type: cancelled by the Receptionist) first.","UC-20, UC-21, UC-25"],
["CBR-79","The cost of goods is outside the system's scope.","UC-09, UC-46"],
["CBR-80","A Missed session earns the PT commission like a CheckedIn one, because the customer's absence is not the PT's fault.","UC-32, UC-46"],
["CBR-81","A session cancelled by the PT under BR-66 earns commission like a CheckedIn one, because the PT has repaid the customer in cash.","UC-35, UC-46"],
["CBR-82",W+"customers do not cancel sessions (UC-39 withdrawn). Historical sessions cancelled ByCustomer keep their stored commission in reports.","UC-39, UC-46"],
["CBR-83","A PT cannot submit a leave request for a shift (GBR-38) in which they still have a Scheduled session; the form lists the blocking sessions with a link to session handling on the PT schedule. While a leave request is Pending or Approved, the PT's free slots in that shift are locked (shown \"leave pending\" / \"leave approved\"), cannot be booked by a PT sale, cannot be used as reschedule or transfer targets, and the PT cannot publish new slots there. A booked session is never hidden by a leave request.","UC-14, UC-21, UC-30, UC-35"],
["CBR-84","A leave request must be submitted before the submission cut-off on the day before the leave (P-12, default 15:00). After the cut-off the system refuses it (MSG192) and the employee informs the Manager directly. Example: leave on Thursday → deadline 15:00 Wednesday.","UC-09, UC-14"],
["CBR-85","There is no approval deadline and no automatic rejection. A Pending request whose leave starts today or tomorrow is flagged \"leave soon\" and listed first; JOB-07 sends the Manager one bell reminder for the Pending requests starting tomorrow. A request whose leave has already started can still be approved under BR-86.","UC-14, UC-15"],
["CBR-86","When a role of a Person becomes Inactive — the employee resigns (UC-13) or the customer profile is deleted (UC-16, UC-17) — every session of that Person's account is signed out immediately. If the Person still has another role that is not Inactive, the account stays Active and from then on serves only that role; otherwise the account becomes Inactive, which is final (DBR-28).","UC-07, UC-13, UC-16, UC-17"],
["CBR-87","An employee's position can change only when no unfinished work remains in the old position: a PT has no Scheduled session, no future slot and no running PT package; a Receptionist has no open shift. Changes to or from Admin follow BR-08.","UC-07, UC-13"],
["CBR-88","Each shift must keep at least P-13 (default 2) PTs on duty after leave is approved.","UC-09, UC-15"],
["CBR-89","The Receptionist also looks after the gym facilities: they view the catalogue, report broken equipment and close repaired requests.","UC-27, UC-28"],
["CBR-90","Each shift must keep at least P-14 (default 1) Receptionist on duty after leave is approved.","UC-09, UC-15"],
["CBR-91","A PT can edit only the private notes and workout/meal plans they created; everyone can edit only their own account profile.","UC-04, UC-33, UC-34, UC-40"],
["CBR-92","A private note about a customer is visible only to the PT who wrote it — even after the customer moves to another PT, the new PT cannot see it.","UC-32, UC-33"],
["CBR-93","After a successful password change in Account Settings (UC-04), every other session of that account is signed out; after a password reset through Forgot Password (UC-03), every session is signed out and a temporary sign-in lock is cleared.","UC-03, UC-04"],
["CBR-94","A verification or recovery code allows P-17 (default 5) wrong entries. On the last wrong entry the code is cancelled and verification for that email is locked for P-18 (default 5) minutes — no entry and no new code during the lock. Requesting a new code is allowed 60 seconds after the previous one; the 5th request within an hour triggers the same lock. A new code always cancels the previous one.","UC-03, UC-04, UC-05, UC-Claim"],
["CBR-95","Staff accounts (Admin, Manager, PT, Receptionist) are created only by the Admin. If the phone number matches an active Person (for example a customer), the staff role is attached to that Person instead of a new Person (CBR-114); if that Person already has an account, no second account is created — the existing account now also serves the staff role (DBR-65). Customer accounts come from exactly two sources: online self sign-up (UC-05) or creation by the Receptionist at the counter (CBR-24). The Admin never creates customer accounts.","UC-05, UC-07, UC-16, UC-20"],
["CBR-96","An account is blocked from signing in only in three cases: it is Inactive because every role of its Person is Inactive (CBR-86), the Admin has locked it, or it is temporarily locked under BR-01.","UC-01, UC-07"],
["CBR-97","An Inactive (stopped) package is no longer sold online or at the counter; running orders and subscriptions of that package are unaffected and still appear on the customer's screens.","UC-10, UC-20, UC-22, UC-36"],
["CBR-98","A voucher used at least once can only be deactivated, never deleted.","UC-12, UC-23"],
["CBR-99","Equipment is never hard-deleted, and management works at two levels: a facility group can only be hidden or shown in the Receptionist catalogue (IsActive), and an individual equipment item is retired (Retired). An item that still has an Open or In Progress maintenance request cannot be retired. A retired item is excluded from quantities and can no longer be reported broken.","UC-27, UC-28"],
["CBR-100","A blog post switched to Inactive disappears from the public site immediately.","UC-06, UC-45"],
["CBR-101","When the Manager approves a maintenance request, the individual equipment item of that request (not the whole facility group) switches to UnderMaintenance automatically, unless the Manager unticks \"Set item to Under maintenance\" because the item can still be used while waiting for the repair.","UC-27, UC-29"],
["CBR-102","When the Receptionist closes a maintenance request, the equipment item returns to Available automatically only if it has no other request still In Progress and it has not been Retired.","UC-27, UC-28"],
["CBR-103","The audit log and audit-related metrics are visible to the Admin only; the Manager's report does not include them.","UC-46, UC-47"],
["CBR-104","Each open day has exactly two duty shifts — morning (opening–13:00) and afternoon (13:00–closing), GBR-38 — derived from the opening hours; there is no manual rostering.","UC-11, UC-25"],
["CBR-105","The Receptionist on duty opens the shift at its start and closes it at its end; every payment taken while the shift is open is recorded in that shift. Counter sales and counter payments are refused while no shift is open (MSG109, MSG110).","UC-20, UC-21, UC-25, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-106","Only the Manager can read customer feedback; PTs and Receptionists cannot. A PT sees only their own monthly average rating (DBR-69).","UC-42, UC-43"],
["CBR-107","Each piece of feedback has a submission time and a read/unread state. There is no reply or resolution workflow — the Manager only reads it. Re-rating the same PT in the same month makes the feedback unread again (DBR-67).","UC-42, UC-43"],
["CBR-108","In their own account a staff member can change only the avatar, email, phone number and password. Personnel details are view-only: full name, date of birth, employee code, position, hire date and employment status for every staff role; a PT also sees specialty, years of experience and commission rate. These details are changed by the Manager (UC-13); position and account status only by the Admin (CBR-109); the employee code never changes (DBR-09). Full name and date of birth are stored once on Person: whether changed by the Manager (UC-13) or the Receptionist (UC-16), the change applies to every role of that Person and is logged (CBR-112). Email and phone number changes follow CBR-110.","UC-04, UC-13"],
["CBR-109","Role, position and account status (active / locked) are never editable in Account Settings. Only the Admin changes an employee's position (UC-07, CBR-87, BR-08) and locks or unlocks an account. A role is added by creating a customer profile (CBR-19, CBR-24) or a staff role (CBR-95) on the Person, never by editing the account. The only automatic changes are CBR-86 and the temporary lock of BR-01.","UC-04, UC-07, UC-13"],
["CBR-110","Changing the email or phone number in Account Settings (UC-04), in any role, requires a 6-digit verification code: for a new email the code is sent to the new email; for a new phone number it is sent to the account's current email. The new value must differ from the current one and is checked for duplicates (DBR-22, DBR-23) before the code is sent and again when it is saved; the value saved is exactly the one the code was issued for (GBR-13). The user may cancel a pending change. Email and phone number are stored on Person, so the change applies to every role. Changes made at the counter by the Receptionist (BR-19) need no code.","UC-04, UC-16"],
["CBR-111","The Dependent profiles tab of Account Settings is shown only when the user is working in the Customer role (CBR-113); it lists, read-only, the Dependent profiles whose guardian phone is the account's phone number, with whether each can use PT services (P-05). A staff role never sees it.","UC-04, UC-16"],
["CBR-112","Changes of email, phone number, avatar and password in Account Settings, and changes of the personal data stored on Person by the Manager or the Receptionist, are written to the audit log as readable sentences (GBR-08) that state the role the user was working in. Passwords and verification codes are never written to the log (DBR-02). If the change is saved but the audit line fails, the user is told (MSG302).","UC-04, UC-08, UC-13, UC-16"],
["CBR-113","A user signs in with email or phone number and password; either one identifies exactly one account (DBR-22, DBR-23, DBR-65). If the account serves more than one role that is not Inactive, the system shows the role selection screen — the staff position or Customer — before opening any home screen. The session holds exactly one role, and every screen and permission follows that role (GBR-10). The user can switch role at any time from the account menu without signing in again; an account with a single role goes straight to that role's home screen.","UC-01, UC-02, UC-04"],
["CBR-114","The phone number identifies the Person. When a customer profile or a staff role is created for a phone number that matches an active Person who does not hold that kind of role (DBR-65), the Receptionist or the Admin checks an identity document and attaches the new role to that Person: no second Person is created, and full name and date of birth are taken from the Person. This happens only in the customer profile form (CBR-19) and in staff account creation (CBR-95); online sign-up never attaches a role to an existing Person (CBR-26) and directs such a phone number to the counter.","UC-05, UC-07, UC-16"],
["CBR-115","A Person must not act in a staff role on their own customer profile: when the signed-in staff role and the customer profile belong to the same Person, the system blocks selling or changing a package, applying a voucher, freezing, editing or deleting the profile, approving its deletion, refunding, and any PT sale, session handling, note or plan in which the same Person is both trainee and PT. Another employee with the required permission performs the action instead.","UC-16, UC-17, UC-18, UC-19, UC-20, UC-21, UC-23, UC-33, UC-34, UC-35"],
["CBR-116","A customer may rate a PT for a month only if, in that month, they (or their couple partner on the same package) have at least one session with that PT closed as CheckedIn or Missed.","UC-32, UC-42"],
["CBR-117","\"Can use the gym\" on a date means: the customer holds a Membership or a DayPass that covers that date and is not frozen on that date. A couple-package session is blocked only when neither member can use the gym. This single definition is used by JOB-04, JOB-08, the customer schedule and bookings, the customer dashboard and the PT dashboard.","UC-19, UC-32, UC-36, UC-41"],
["CBR-118","Quick-create customer on the sales screen (UC-20): Self profile — full name (DBR-01), date of birth (DBR-04), phone number (DBR-17) not used by any existing customer, and email (format and DBR-23) are required; the account is created under CBR-24 / CBR-31. Dependent profile — full name, date of birth, guardian name (2–50 characters), relationship (required, up to 30 characters) and guardian phone are required; no email and no account. The profile starts as New with a new customer code.","UC-16, UC-20"],
["CBR-119","Start date of a membership package or day pass: if the customer still holds a membership that has not expired, the new package starts the day after it ends (chained, not selectable); otherwise it starts today or on a date chosen up to 7 days ahead. After an online purchase the customer may move the start date of an unused membership package once, to a date from today to today + 7 days; the end date is recomputed from the package duration.","UC-20, UC-22, UC-41"],
["CBR-120","A customer whose profile is Frozen or Inactive cannot create, cancel or pay an online order.","UC-22, UC-PAY"],
["CBR-121","Annual leave uses the yearly quota P-23 minus Approved and Pending annual days. If the remaining quota is smaller than the days requested, the system proposes splitting the request into an Annual part and an Unpaid part; the employee must accept the split, and the balance is re-checked when the request is saved (MSG193, MSG194). One notification is sent for the whole request.","UC-14, UC-15"],
["CBR-122","Operational report: From and To dates are required, From ≤ To, with no limit on the range; ranges up to 62 days are charted per day, longer ranges per month. The CSV export contains exactly the displayed report (GBR-33). The Admin report adds audit metrics (CBR-103).","UC-46, UC-47"],
]
